<article class="env-definition" id="04N5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04N5">Definition <span data-tag="04N5">66.9.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$ be a point of $X$. We define the <em>dimension of $X$ at $x$</em> to be the element $\dim _ x(X) \in \{ 0, 1, 2, \ldots , \infty \} $ such that $\dim _ x(X) = \dim _ u(U)$ for any (equivalently some) pair $(a : U \to X, u)$ consisting of an étale morphism $a : U \to X$ from a scheme to $X$ and a point $u \in U$ with $a(u) = x$. See Definition <a href="/tag/04RC" data-tag="04RC">66.7.5</a>, Lemma <a href="/tag/04N2" data-tag="04N2">66.7.4</a>, and Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/04N4" data-tag="04N4">35.21.2</a>. </p>
</article>